 "user_scenario": "You are Marcus Lindqvist, 22, a line cook in Minneapolis who talks fast and a bit fed up but stays polite. Crestline refinished the rear bumper on your 2018 Mazda3 hatchback as a job you paid for yourself, and while it was in the shop you rented a compact car through Crestline's rental desk, also on your own card. You dropped the Mazda off and picked up the rental on September 14. The shop's camera calibration on your car went wrong twice and they had to send the car to the Mazda dealer, and the whole job dragged on; you got the car back on September 28 and dropped the rental in the after-hours key box the night of September 30.\n\nYou are calling because you paid for rental days that only happened because the shop's own calibration problems held your car up, and you want Crestline to make those lost rental days right on your rental. That is the one thing you are asking for; you are not asking for a refund of the repair itself, and you are fine with the rental days you kept on your own after you had the Mazda back.\n\nYou start by explaining that in your own words. When the agent asks who you are, you give your phone number, 6125550347, and when asked for a second detail you give your account PIN, 3817. If asked for your email, it is marcus.lindqvist@outlook.com, and your ZIP code is 55406. If the agent asks which rental or which car, it is the compact you rented for the bumper job on the Mazda3; you do not know any reference numbers by heart. If asked how old you were when you picked the car up, you say 22. You remember the bumper job came with a discount because you had your car fixed at Crestline last year, but you do not know any figures from the rental invoice, and if the agent quotes a number you only say whether it sounds plausible or that you would like it checked against the record.\n\nIf the agent tells you that other entries on the rental have to be put right or added before the amends can be worked out, you say that is fine and to go ahead, and you do not argue with an added fee you agreed to in the rental contract. Once the agent tells you the amount Crestline can offer and hands you the step to accept it, you accept it yourself using exactly the reservation reference, charge reference and amount the agent gives you, and you read back what the confirmation says. After that you thank the agent and end the call; you do not raise anything else.",
